Z||000000||whamel||08-28-2000||12:00 AM||||I have to say, this was probably the best Fiero spotters weekend I have had yet.  On Friday evening I saw a beautiful black GT on US-33 headed into Columbus, OH, and on Sunday  evening I saw a Burgandy GT on I-69 headed from Michigan down towards Ft. Wayne, and when I got to Ft. Wayne I saw one of the nicest white GT's I have seen in a long time at the gas station off US-30 in Indiana.  That really made my day...only could have been better if I would have actually been driving my fiero so these people wouldn't have wondered why I was staring at them like an idiot!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>This makes up for the stupid high winds (I wonder if they'll say it was a tornado) taking out my power all weekend so I couldn't get any work done on MY GT.  ARGH!  I had to break down and put it in the shop since I'm running out of time.  No damage to any of the Fiero's (whew), but I have 1/2 of one of my trees sitting on top of my house now. <BR>Thanks,<BR>Wade||||reg||10
